    gettingStartedBody: "# Welcome to GitDesktop\n\nGitDesktop is a desktop Git client for status, staging, branches, history, diffs, and sync, with pull requests, GitHub Actions, issues, discussions, releases, and repository insights. AI agent sessions are available when AI features are enabled.\n\n## Get started\n\n- **Git is required.** GitDesktop uses your system `git`; every operation is standard Git.\n- **GitHub features require GitHub CLI `gh`.** Install and sign in to use pull requests, issues, Actions, and repository settings. Sign in from Settings → Accounts or run `gh auth login`. The app does not store access tokens.\n- **Bitbucket Cloud** connects from Settings → Accounts with an Atlassian API token.\n- **Choose your interface language.** Select English or Simplified Chinese in Settings → General. The choice applies immediately and is saved for the next launch.\n\n## Open a repository\n\n- **Open repository**: choose an existing Git repository folder.\n- **Clone repository**: paste a URL or choose from GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket.\n- **Create repository**: create a local repository, optionally with a README, `.gitignore`, and license.",
